OL,3,ACelebrity loses injunction bid but will
OL,4,Astay anonymous pending appeal
OL,5,
OL,6,FA celebrity who asked the High Court to
OL,7,Fpermanently prevent two news
OL,8,Forganisations from publishing his
OL,9,Fidentity and allegations of sexual
OL,10,Fmisconduct has lost his case, with the
OL,11,Fcourt saying the man's claim for an
OL,12,Finjunction was denied.
OL,14,FBut the judge said a temporary
OL,15,Finjunction preventing the man from
OL,16,Fbeing named and the allegations
OL,17,Fpublished should remain in place, in
OL,18,Forder to allow the celebrity to appeal
OL,19,Fagainst the judgment, with anonymity
OL,20,Fand reporting restrictions remaining in
OL,21,Fforce during the period allowed for any
OL,22,Fappeal.
OL,23,APub: 03-NovQpppppppppppppppppppppG10/19
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,162,160,200,105,0,100
PN,11911
SC,0011
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1793728094
OL,1,W5j 5Q7+j 55"k#j 5w;js1
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-.*,%-,* *,%%**,$ ,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,ACelebrity loses injunction bid but will
OL,4,Astay anonymous pending appeal
OL,5,
OL,6,FITN and the Guardian have said they
OL,7,Fbelieve it is in the public interest to
OL,8,Fpublish allegations that the man abused
OL,9,Fhis status to engage, or attempt to
OL,10,Fengage, in "inappropriate sexual
OL,11,Factivities with a large number of girls
OL,12,Fand young women".
OL,14,FThe man, who denies the allegations,
OL,15,Fsaid any publication would be "highly
OL,16,Flikely" to lead him to kill himself,
OL,17,Fand that the court should prevent any
OL,18,Fpublication or broadcast.
OL,23,APub: 03-NovQpppppppppppppppppppppG11/19
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
